  "details": "The ears of my character, previously in the beta version of physbones and the first official release did not have this issue.\nThe ears are parented to the upper chest and using a parent constraint to bind them to the head. (getting around the head shrinking in first person, allowing you to see them in first person)\nBy default I scale the ears down to zero on the root bone that has the parent constraint, the bone below the root has the physbone script.\nUpon the animator being loaded I have an animation that sets them back to 1 instantly. (because using the parent constraint in this way causes the ears to look weird in the avatar preview)\nIn newer versions of the sdk this causes instant stability loss in unity playmode, whereas the version I used that was the first official sdk release does not lose stability at all in playmode.\nIn game upon the avatar being loaded for anyone, the ears will freak out unless already hidden, but anyone else that joins after will see the broken physbones.\nIn game this can be fixed by hiding then unhiding the ears. (which is an animation that scales them down to 0 then back to 1) \nI assume this issue is due to the scale not being correctly applied when loaded, as the animation set them back to 1 before the physbones script started?",
